From: WBR Runtime Maintainers <wbr-runtime@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize LocalMapping state read before the first keyframe

Base-commit: 4452a3c4ab75b1cde34e5505a36ec3f9edcdc4c4

The D435i file runner calls System::GetTimeFromIMUInit after TrackStereo,
including before LocalMapping has processed a keyframe. GetCurrKFTime
checks an indeterminate mpCurrentKeyFrame and may dereference garbage.
Initialize it to nullptr so the existing no-keyframe branch returns zero.

GetTimeFromIMUInit also subtracts mFirstTs before checking the atlas IMU
flag. Initialize that timestamp to zero in the same clock domain as the
keyframe timestamps, avoiding a second indeterminate read on this path.
InitializeIMU still replaces it with the first keyframe timestamp.

This extends the recorded Pi patch 4 by initializing mFirstTs as well.
It does not address Settings printing, reset lifetime or thread safety.
The saved report names SIGSEGV in GetCurrKFTime; no raw gdb trace or
successful patched Pi rerun is available in the inspected evidence.

---
 include/LocalMapping.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/LocalMapping.h b/include/LocalMapping.h
--- a/include/LocalMapping.h
+++ b/include/LocalMapping.h
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@
     unsigned int mInitSect;
     unsigned int mIdxInit;
     unsigned int mnKFs;
-    double mFirstTs;
+    double mFirstTs = 0.0;
     int mnMatchesInliers;
 
     // For debugging (erase in normal mode)
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@
 
     std::list<KeyFrame*> mlNewKeyFrames;
 
-    KeyFrame* mpCurrentKeyFrame;
+    KeyFrame* mpCurrentKeyFrame = nullptr;
 
     std::list<MapPoint*> mlpRecentAddedMapPoints;
 
